Abstract = {The study aimed to show discourses and practices articulated around body
   education in parks and playgrounds in the city of Campinas in 1940-1959.
   Through historical research, it concludes that children's parks and
   playgrounds were important institutions for care, education, culture and
   recreation for children, designed and oriented as a political and
   educational project to control children, but also to establish local and
   national identities still not consolidated as modern, urban and
   rational.},
