Year = {2022},
Volume = {14},
Number = {3},
Month = {FEB},
Abstract = {The underlying cause of the problem with parking is the imbalance
   between demand and supply in key areas where demand for parking is high,
   but parking is limited due to excessive land prices. Newly-developed
   automated multi-storey parking facilities are able to automatically pick
   up and place cars on different storeys, with minimal requirements on
   space. In the paper we concentrate on Automated Parking Systems and
   their malfunction rate. Specifically, we analyzed two automated systems
   located in the Czech Republic, in the towns of Brno and SlanATIN SMALL
   LETTER Y WITH ACUTE. We employed time series and various testing
   hypotheses to compare the malfunction rate of the systems, and used
   information from practice. We conclude with an evaluation and a brief
   description of the optimization of systems and the use of innovative
   tools.},
